{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "_about": "The single declaration authority for the plan: its tables, the expression VM's opcodes, the stdlib roster, and the enum vocabularies. plan/build.rs generates the row structs, the canonical encoder, the validating decoder, the opcode and stdlib enums, and FORMAT_DIGEST from this file. Nothing here is hand-mirrored anywhere else. Kernel node types, props, and style rows are NOT declared here: plan rows carry the kernel's ordinals as numbers, and the crates that give them meaning take the vocabulary from exact-kernel (LLP 1004 D2).",
  "_codecs": "u8 | u16 | u32 | i32 | f64 | bool | str (u32 index into the string pool) | enum:<Name> (u8 ordinal) | idx:<table> (u32 row index, validated) | opt:<table> (u32 row index or NONE = 0xFFFFFFFF) | range:<table> (u32 start + u32 len, validated) | code (u32 offset + u32 len into the code pool, validated as well-formed bytecode) | bytes (u32 offset + u32 len into the data pool)",
  "_tables": "Document order is significant: nodes and regions with the same parent are ordered by `order`; an arm's content is every node and region whose `arm` names it; a node with no parent inside an arm is one of the arm's roots.",
  "tables": [
    { "name": "types", "fields": [
      { "name": "kind", "codec": "enum:TypeKind" },
      { "name": "elem", "codec": "opt:types" },
      { "name": "fields", "codec": "range:fields" },
      { "name": "name", "codec": "str" }
    ]},
    { "name": "fields", "fields": [
      { "name": "name", "codec": "str" },
      { "name": "ty", "codec": "idx:types" }
    ]},
    { "name": "slots", "fields": [
      { "name": "name", "codec": "str" },
      { "name": "ty", "codec": "idx:types" },
      { "name": "init", "codec": "code" }
    ]},
    { "name": "derives", "fields": [
      { "name": "name", "codec": "str" },
      { "name": "ty", "codec": "idx:types" },
      { "name": "body", "codec": "code" }
    ]},
    { "name": "resources", "fields": [
      { "name": "name", "codec": "str" },
      { "name": "source", "codec": "str" },
      { "name": "args", "codec": "range:args" },
      { "name": "ty", "codec": "idx:types" },
      { "name": "initial", "codec": "bytes" }
    ]},
    { "name": "args", "fields": [
      { "name": "expr", "codec": "code" }
    ]},
    { "name": "actions", "fields": [
      { "name": "name", "codec": "str" },
      { "name": "params", "codec": "range:params" },
      { "name": "writes", "codec": "range:writes" },
      { "name": "body", "codec": "code" }
    ]},
    { "name": "params", "fields": [
      { "name": "name", "codec": "str" },
      { "name": "ty", "codec": "idx:types" }
    ]},
    { "name": "writes", "fields": [
      { "name": "slot", "codec": "idx:slots" }
    ]},
    { "name": "timers", "fields": [
      { "name": "interval_ms", "codec": "u32" },
      { "name": "action", "codec": "idx:actions" }
    ]},
    { "name": "regions", "fields": [
      { "name": "kind", "codec": "enum:RegionKind" },
      { "name": "parent", "codec": "opt:nodes" },
      { "name": "arm", "codec": "opt:arms" },
      { "name": "order", "codec": "u32" },
      { "name": "subject", "codec": "code" },
      { "name": "key", "codec": "code" },
      { "name": "arms", "codec": "range:arms" }
    ]},
    { "name": "arms", "fields": [
      { "name": "region", "codec": "idx:regions" }
    ]},
    { "name": "nodes", "fields": [
      { "name": "node_type", "codec": "u8" },
      { "name": "parent", "codec": "opt:nodes" },
      { "name": "arm", "codec": "opt:arms" },
      { "name": "order", "codec": "u32" },
      { "name": "bindings", "codec": "range:bindings" },
      { "name": "handlers", "codec": "range:handlers" }
    ]},
    { "name": "bindings", "fields": [
      { "name": "kind", "codec": "enum:BindingKind" },
      { "name": "id", "codec": "u16" },
      { "name": "expr", "codec": "code" }
    ]},
    { "name": "handlers", "fields": [
      { "name": "event", "codec": "enum:EventKind" },
      { "name": "action", "codec": "idx:actions" },
      { "name": "args", "codec": "range:args" }
    ]}
  ],
  "_enums": "Wire ordinal is the 0-based index. An unknown ordinal is a typed decode rejection.",
  "enums": {
    "TypeKind": ["number", "bool", "string", "unit", "option", "list", "record"],
    "RegionKind": ["when", "match", "each"],
    "BindingKind": ["prop", "style"],
    "EventKind": ["press", "change"]
  },
  "_opcodes": "The expression VM: a stack machine over values with a small locals stack (`BindLocal` pops into it, `LoadLocal` copies from it, `DropLocal` pops it) for names an inline `match` binds. Each opcode names its operand layout; the decoder validates framing and every index operand. `depth` operands count enclosing instance scopes (0 = innermost). Type inference guarantees stack discipline; the VM still traps, never UB.",
  "opcodes": [
    { "name": "Number", "operands": ["f64"] },
    { "name": "Bool", "operands": ["u8"] },
    { "name": "Str", "operands": ["str"] },
